mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5168674Z     "The common normalized, countably additive POVM and the prefix-preserving action of G are candidate premises, not derived native laws.",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5170320Z     "The result applies only to selection based on this history; a separate quantum selective instrument or extra source/reference information is not covered.",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5171961Z     "The proof relies on countable additivity and cylinder-generated access; finitely additive extensions or tail variables not measurable in the generated sigma algebra F are not covered."
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5173065Z   ],
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5173370Z   "observations": [
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5174432Z     "The divisibility of the connected compact Lie group G = U(A) correctly forces any homomorphism to a finite permutation group to be trivial, without requiring a continuity assumption (Section 3).",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5176387Z     "The extension from finite prefixes to the full infinite history correctly applies the pi-system uniqueness theorem to the real and imaginary parts of the finite complex measures comprising the POVM (Section 4).",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5178466Z     "The total-variation approximation lemma correctly establishes that any contrast in the limit history must already appear in some finite joint prefix, avoiding the assumption of a uniform convergence rate (Section 4).",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5180828Z     "The control demonstrating that individual symbol blindness is insufficient correctly justifies the necessity of analyzing complete joint prefixes rather than individual marginals (Section 5).",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5183214Z     "The control regarding the encoding of a supplied oriented register correctly shows that such an encoding must break the finite-prefix equivariance assumption, preventing the silent smuggling of an orientation (Section 5).",
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5185896Z     "The document successfully passes the admission gate by resolving the specific proposed source of the missing diffuse orientation record without claiming a native interaction, physical completion, or new mathematical priority (Section 6)."
mathematical-review	Independent Gemini argument review	2026-10-16T19:40:52.5187518Z   ]
